# What the gate's Opengrep step (`check.sh` step 3e) does not scan, in
# gitignore syntax, anchored at the repository root.  Named to Opengrep by
# --semgrepignore-filename, which also REPLACES its built-in default list:
# that list skipped 212 of the 522 tracked Rust, Kotlin, Python and shell
# files outside test-vectors/: the crates' `tests/` directories and the Android
# shell's `src/test/` [2026-11-20].  So the list is this
# file's and nothing else's.
#
# Files git ignores are not scanned either way: Opengrep takes its targets
# from git, so the build trees and the generated bindings are named below
# for the reader rather than for the tool.

# the canonical vectors and their generator's output: data, not code
/test-vectors/

# build output, cargo's and gradle's
target/
/crates/mobile/android/app/build/
/crates/mobile/android/build/

# the Kotlin binding uniffi generates (`mobile/android/tools/build-native.sh`)
/crates/mobile/android/app/src/generated/

# the symlinks into ../FuerosNet-output, which is output and never source
/runs
/conformance-review
